            <div xml:id="d721">

                <pb facs="0867" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg773"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">353.115V13/28: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dearing</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-05T15:00:00-05:00">February 5, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>8. Your 11, February 3. The Department has discussed the situation in reference
                    to the establishment of an alleged monopoly of the refining of crude oil with a
                    representative of the Vacuum Oil Company who has asked us to take the matter up
                    with the Portuguese Government through the Legation at Lisbon.</p>
                <p>Although it is not believed that this Government could appropriately object in
                    principle to the establishment of an oil monopoly in Portugal you are authorized
                    to explain orally to the appropriate Portuguese officials that this Government
                    regrets to see monopolies created in other countries, when the result thereof
                    works an injury to American interests established there for many years in good
                    faith under existing laws.</p>
                <p>You may, in your discretion, orally inform the British Ambassador of the position
                    of this Government as expressed above. The Department will be pleased to learn
                    what action the British Ambassador is taking in reference to this question and
                    the grounds upon which such action is predicated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
